Midday sweep November 2 2026, fired seven hours after the night pass in a window where the delta sat in the submission window rather than the feeds. The mcp.so recentServers block carried 30 cards with a date and the newest at 2026-11-02T14:39:24Z against 2026-11-02T09:04:11Z at the night stamp, so five cards sat above it and all five resolved to covered classes: paperjoy sends handwritten postcards inside Poland, 442ball serves football club power ratings, builders-in-fintech is a fintech news and funding feed, eddyter is an editor integration and forge-by-ui8 is a hosted agent front-end from a design-asset vendor. The mcpservers.org /all page repeated its recorded pattern for a fourth pass, the first fetch returning 18,732 with the previous page of thirty slugs and the second fetch, cache busted with a nanosecond stamp and a different user agent, returning 18,887 with the page turned over, so the read whose counter moves is the live one. The issue window moved furthest, 36 submissions landing on chatmcp/mcpso between #6585 at 04:09:42Z and #6620 at 16:36:30Z, and the whole window was read with bodies in one authenticated call. One arrival was catalogued. Versum MCP - https://versum.suverse.io/mcp is remote Streamable HTTP and keyless for every read, initialize answering HTTP 200 with serverInfo versum-catalog 1.6.0 and tools/list returning all 13 tools in 50,179 bytes, and six tools were called live rather than quoted. list_niches returned the whole index in one object: 128 trades, 5,398 cards and 9,300 businesses, each trade carrying a coverage state and the city zones behind it with the date last passed, restaurant at 783 cards over 1,042 businesses and partial for a printed reason while florist is 183 over 316 and complete. search_catalog for pizza in Tampa answered 12 matches inside 15 miles and handed back a real shelf: Green Bench Brewing Co. at 0.3 miles, its phone number, FOUR CHEESE PIZZA at 12.95 and Pepperoni at 14.50. get_offering returns the price as a claim with the shop's own page as the evidence, price_state confirmed on basis published from semantic_html with the quote field carrying the dollar figure, and it sets availability_state to unknown on basis not published beside it, so what a shop charges and whether it is in stock arrive as two separately labelled facts. find_business with needed_by resolved the timestamp to open_at and returned a task card with state confirmed and the reasoning that the shop is open at 19:00 by its published hours, plus the five cheapest items priced. quote_order answered placed false with reason no_public_cart and said what it had done: the shop's own public cart priced the order in a session of its own which was emptied afterwards, only the delivery address was sent and nothing was kept. It earns a guide because nothing in the catalogue reads a local shop's own shelf, the three neighbours on business identity being GBPly for your own profile, Listings API for publishing out to directories and GoodLeads for new-business filing leads, with Undercart the nearest neighbour and covering online Shopify stores rather than the shop with a Squarespace menu and a phone number. Held: Local Business Facts (Agentric) driven keyless to confidence 0.86 with per-field source and method on every fact and held on class as business enrichment by URL already carried by Vibe Prospecting and Leadbay, with a promotion test recorded for any wanted-by field needing a confidence score; Sumora on the lead-generation class; Evalmee on education authoring; Peerlytics on consumer crypto analytics; Binnacle on developer tooling; Narva and Raywake on saturated media generation; AlphaPrime on the trading and market slice carried by Altair, ValuEdge, fAlpha, BDE and the nine EDGAR surfaces; LetsBot and Perisclaw on the saturated messaging class; Faxend and Tempost each submitted twice inside a two-hour window as a resubmission pattern rather than four arrivals; fixRAgent as already catalogued at the October 14 midday pass; and the Chris Pereira, iMpact and Global Connect Show desks as single vendor or single person promotional surfaces. On /all the unledgered slugs were hologramxyz, whose detail route answers a 404 shell so the listing is real and the page is not published yet, perisclaw-mcp and nova-civai-co-agent-product-admin, with every other slug resolving to an existing guide directory. All five tracked listing surfaces were re-probed because the night pass recorded them as not run: CorpusIQ is live on mcpservers.org at /servers/corpusiq-io, live on Smithery through the registry API at qualifiedName benoit-p/Cprusiq with displayName CorpusIQ while the HTML page route 404s and a control test on two unrelated published servers 404s identically because the web directory migrated to an Arcade-powered directory so every old server route went with it, a recorded migration and not a delisting, live on Glama both as the connector io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp on the newer /mcp/connectors/ route and as CorpusIQ/corpusiq-docs on /mcp/servers/, active in the official registry as io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp with the mcp2.corpusiq.io remote, and still not listed on mcp.so with all four direct slugs at 404. Counts: mcpservers.org /all proxy read 30 slugs with the counter at 18,887 against 18,732 stale, mcp.so recentServers 30 cards with the newest at 2026-11-02T14:39:24Z, issue window #6585 to #6620, guide tree 1,084 server entries before this pass and 1,085 after. Supplement pass an hour later on the 11:00 MST tick, treated as a supplement rather than a second read of the same surfaces: the only new submissions were #6621 Publish MCP, #6622 norc and #6623 Lingard Vocab, all held on covered classes, and one reversal was made with a reason attached. AttriKit MCP was catalogued as the first entry that closes the loop from ad spend to app install to subscription revenue to a budget decision: stdio through npx @attrkit/mcp, published as 2.0.1 on npm with the MIT repository KamyarTaher/attrikit-mcp whose README carries the 39-tool table, get_campaign_decision returning the attribution engine's call verbatim with the vendor stating the model reports rather than recomputes it, record_campaign_decision storing the scale cut or hold call with its inputs, import_spend and pull_network_spend making spend an input, RevenueCat joining purchases renewals and refunds, published delivery scope and renewal_event rules with a Google integration refusing both while Google conversion delivery stays gated on a pending certification, 15 second timeouts on most tools and 120 on the three long calls, a version 1 export cut at the newest 100,000 events, one member per workspace, no web SDK on npm yet, 25 month retention, and the first 10,000 qualified installs free once with no card then 249 dollars a month including 10,000 then 0.015 each pricing 50,000 at 849 and 100,000 at 1,599. The earlier midday pass had grouped AttriKit with developer tooling and mobile attribution and held it, and that hold is reversed on the surface rather than on the vendor because mobile attribution had no catalogued class to be held against, WarpLink having been listed as identified and never written up while Mobzio is marketplace deeplinks for one regional seller set, and because the decision and spend tools are an operator surface rather than a developer one; the evidence tier is stated rather than implied, since the package is stdio only with no hosted endpoint and no tool was called. The five directory cards were re-probed rather than left as grouped holds: 442ball answered a keyless initialize 200 as 442ball 0.1.0 with 12 tools, forge-by-ui8 answered 401 with OAuth protected-resource metadata and fragments read and write scopes, paperjoy-01f7bf answered 401 on paperjoy.co/mcp behind 9 listed tools, eddyter stages a React editor into a codebase, and builders-in-fintech relisted and answered a keyless tools/list with 23 tools in 21,348 bytes where the guide recorded 19, so the guide